#567 fbctrlcmdkill -- PRE-TABLE ADDENDUM for kill table 3, written 2026-10-19 BEFORE the table runs (this file's mtime is
the order proof).  INSTRUMENT: probe v3 (106 rows; the session scratchpad's fbctrl_cmd_probe.v3.py, built by
mk_probe_v3.py from v2 and frozen into the table's directory).  BASELINE: the fix, in /tmp/gx567.  Its legs before this
table (scratchpad v3legs/): the fix 106/106, HEAD's binary 42/106.

V3 CLOSES THE WIDTH x BOUND-EDGE CLASS IN ONE DIFF (kill table 3a measured all seven of its open cells ESCAPING v2,
99/99 each): accept 2 and refuse 3 now held at EVERY width --
    accept 2 (GET; its dispatch zeroes X1):  sb A:get    sh A:edges   sw L, seeds   sd A:edges
    refuse 3:                                sb R:sb3    sh R:edges   sw R:3        sd R:edges
-- and the latch's persistence: T2 now accepts a NOP and reads COMMAND between its first and second refusals.

THE TABLE re-runs every mutant built -- tables 1 (11), 1b (5), 2a (9) and 3a (7): 32 -- and both null media.

PREDICTIONS
* every one of the 32 RED.
* the seven table-3a escapes, with the rows v3 added:
    E15_sdnodisp   acc sd get x1 (0x7b: the sd GET is stored, never dispatched)               -> 105/106
    E16_sdbound0   acc sd get x1 (0x7b), acc edges quiet (1): sd 2 refused, announced         -> 104/106
    E17_shbound1   acc sh get x1 (0x7b), acc edges quiet (1): sh 2 refused, announced         -> 104/106
    E18_sdbound3   edge alive, edge cmd: sd 3 is accepted and reaches default:; sessions
                   clean (23).  `edge once' stays green -- the sh 3 announce prints first     -> 103/106
    E19_shbound3   edge alive, edge cmd, edge once ('-': sh 3, the session's first write,
                   kills it before any announce); sessions clean (23)                         -> 102/106
    E20_latchacc   two once (0x3,0x5: the NOP resets the latch, so 5 announces)              -> 105/106
    E21_latchread  two once (0x3,0x5: the read resets the latch)                             -> 105/106
* the null media: CONTROL=FAILED and 16/106 -- the eleven noset rows and FIVE announce counts (v3 adds `acc edges
  quiet'), every one reading 0 on a session that never started; `acc set res' and `sessions clean' among the red.
